SUMMARY:Living History Day at Petaluma Adobe State Park
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time and experience life in Alta California at Living History Day. Meet vaqueros\, traders\, cooks\, and craftspeople as they bring history to life through engaging demonstrations and storytelling.    Enjoy hands-on blacksmithing and woodworking demonstrations\, play traditional historical games\, and bring a picnic to enjoy on the grounds. Families can also participate in the Junior Rangers program—bring your logbook to earn a badge and stamp.    Admission is affordable\, with activities included for all ages. This interactive event offers a fun and educational way to explore California’s rich past in an authentic historic setting.
URL:https://www.sonoma.com/event/living-history-day-at-petaluma-adobe-state-historic-park/
LOCATION:3325 Adobe Rd.,  Petaluma, CA, 94954, United States
CATEGORIES:Educational,Family Friendly,Outdoors,Sonoma County
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://winecountry-media.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2026/05/02232240/Andrew-Crockett-and-Troy-Dunham-w-saddle-by-JHanson.jpg
END:VEVENT
